One thing worth noting: this pattern — expired session → null → unhandled NPE — tends to appear in more than one place once it shows up in an auth flow. The `getUserProfile()` call is probably not the only method that retrieves session-dependent data without a null guard. If you want, I can take a look at the broader `AuthService` class (or wherever session lookups happen) and flag any other spots with the same vulnerability. That way you're patching the root cause rather than playing whack-a-mole as the same issue surfaces elsewhere.

